    "body": "Having installed this branch for a bit, I'm starting to feel that we shouldn't be showing ms time data by default. This is particularly the case when a command has been running for minutes. At that point, the millisecond granularity doesn't provide much value to the average user:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4658208/70737361-530f8700-1ce0-11ea-8a87-c03c39e7be0d.png)\r\n\r\nEven for shorter commands, I find it to be noisy:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4658208/70737585-da5cfa80-1ce0-11ea-8326-fc827f5865a1.png)\r\n\r\nI was thinking that for durations of <1s, we should show milliseconds, and otherwise hide milliseconds unless a `show_milliseconds` configuration option is enabled.\r\n\r\nThoughts?",
    "state": "COMMENTED",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/696#pullrequestreview-331423814",
